// the texel (its four neighbours half a texel away), and only where the texel straddles the shore (the
// samples differ in sign): such a texel's sea, sand and shelf shares are what it covers. A texel wholly on
// land or at sea keeps the point's own bands (0): the distance-field width (fp × GR_LAND_M) is far too wide
