#endif
// The cloud over a ray's inscatter in_ (whole path, transmittance trans): it hides the
// inscatter behind it and is seen through the air in front (transmittance tf). The share in
// front follows the extinction (1 − T), so a far band keeps the blue haze in front of it and
// is not reddened by the whole limb path (which turned distant bands khaki). Seen from above
// the deck, a cloud may not come out darker than most of the haze it hides: past the limb a
// dusk-lit band in front of the brightest air read as black streaks. From below (overcast)
// it may: there the hidden part is the blue sky.
vec3 clFront(vec3 in_, vec3 trans, vec3 tf, vec4 cl, float above){
  float front=clamp((1.-grLum(tf))/max(1.-grLum(trans),1e-4),0.,1.);
  vec3 hidden=in_*cl.a*(1.-front);
